  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Your teacher will give you a <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/aaf42413c671790da0b748421bfdfedd4a5c7243">set of cards</link> containing descriptions of situations and graphs. Match each situation with a graph that represents it. Record your matches and be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>
<para>Use the cards to answer questions 1–4. Match each graph representation to the description of the situation characterized by exponential change. Then choose the relationship between the number of years since purchase and the value.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="99c6e94c-ca45-45b1-b4e2-feab4907b466" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"> <!--Q#1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ee94e163-7f73-4cab-8d33-69086729ff4f" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="A car loses \(\frac14\) of its value every year after purchase." data-solution-options="[&quot;The value of a stock doubles approximately every 4 years.&quot;, &quot;A car loses \\(\\frac14\\) of its value every year after purchase.&quot;, &quot;The value of a stock triples roughly every 8 years.&quot;, &quot;A laptop loses \\(\\frac25\\) of its value every year after purchase.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the description of exponential change shown in the graph. </para>
      <image alt="" class="img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="283" role="presentation" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/9bbfaea14fa34c45968c0ce2f4841e93c52b7ff8" width="300"/></problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! A car loses \(\frac14\) of its value every year after purchase.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.--> <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE --> 
</div>
</div>
<!--Q#2-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What is the equation for this graph? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(v = p(1 - \frac14)^t\)</para>
    <para>\(v = p(\frac34)^t\)</para>
    <para>Where:</para>
    <para>\(v = \)value of the car after \(t\) years.</para>
    <para>\(p =\) initial price of the car.</para>
    <para>\(t =\) time in years.</para>
    <para>\(14 =\) fraction by which the car loses its value every year.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="3605d9fd-0f46-4702-8f63-b16eec3147ea" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"> <!--Q#3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4f069820-3994-4438-ad4e-1d04aced19a6" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="The value of a stock triples roughly every 8 years." data-solution-options="[&quot;The value of a stock doubles approximately every 4 years.&quot;, &quot;A car loses \\(\\frac14\\) of its value every year after purchase.&quot;, &quot;The value of a stock triples roughly every 8 years.&quot;, &quot;A laptop loses \\(\\frac25\\) of its value every year after purchase.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the description of exponential change shown in the graph. </para>
      <image alt="" class="img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="283" role="presentation" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/341268b726cdfab16cddb704ac3bb3710ee41bac" width="300"/> </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The value of a stock triples roughly every 8 years.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<!--Q#4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What is the equation for this graph? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(v = p(3)^{\frac{t}{8}}\)</para>
    <para>Where:</para>
    <para>\(v\) is the current value of the stock after t years.</para>
    <para>\(p\) is the initial value of the stock.</para>
    <para>\(t \)is the number of years since the initial value.</para>
    <para>In this equation, we raise 3 to the power of \((\frac{t}{8})\) to calculate the value after \(t\) years. This represents the stock tripling in value approximately every 8 years.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="12d8c69c-da8f-4925-9cbd-09280a2c9acd" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"> <!--Q#5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="425179bb-4b3d-40b6-b1e9-35c21f92dc6a" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="The value of a stock doubles approximately every 4 years." data-solution-options="[&quot;The value of a stock doubles approximately every 4 years.&quot;, &quot;A car loses \\(\\frac14\\) of its value every year after purchase.&quot;, &quot;The value of a stock triples roughly every 8 years.&quot;, &quot;A laptop loses \\(\\frac25\\) of its value every year after purchase.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Choose the description of exponential change shown in the graph. </para>
      <image alt="" class="img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="283" role="presentation" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7934f218dc3c293fb362c0bfe213e7ba74624e0f" width="300"/></problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The value of a stock doubles approximately every 4 years.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.--> <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
